11. Women of childbearing age who have a negative pregnancy test within 14 days before treatment. Female patients of childbearing age, and male patients with partners of childbearing age must agree to use at least one medically recognized contraceptive method (such as surgical sterilization, oral contraceptives, intrauterine device, sexual abstinence or barrier contraception combined with spermicide, etc.) during study treatment and within at least 6 months after the last dose of investigational drug;
